      content:
          'A 22-year-old male is transferred to the ventilator-capable acute inpatient rehabilitation unit 3 weeks after sustaining a C3 ASIA A spinal cord injury from a diving accident in a shallow lake. He underwent emergent intubation at the scene, posterior cervical fusion C2-C5, and tracheostomy placement on post-injury day 7. He is currently ventilator-dependent 24 hours per day via a cuffed #8 Shiley tracheostomy on assist-control mode (TV 700 mL, RR 14, FiO2 0.30, PEEP 5). He is alert, communicates by mouthing words and using eye gaze, and appears engaged but anxious.',
