    Section(
      title: 'History & Systems Review:',
      content:
          '- **Mechanism**: Dove headfirst into shallow water (estimated 3-4 feet deep) at a lake party; immediate quadriplegia and apnea; bystander initiated rescue breathing\n- **Surgical**: Posterior C2-C5 fusion with lateral mass screws; tracheostomy day 7 (failed extubation attempt day 5 due to absent respiratory drive)\n- **Neurological**: C3 ASIA A -- no motor or sensory function below C3; no sacral sparing; only preserved function is neck flexion/extension (C1-C2), shoulder shrug (C3-C4 partial on right only, trapezius 2/5 right, 0/5 left)\n- **Respiratory**: Completely ventilator-dependent; no spontaneous respiratory effort observed; diaphragm paralysis confirmed (C3-C5 phrenic nerve involvement)\n- **Current Ventilator Settings**: AC mode, TV 700 mL, RR 14, FiO2 0.30, PEEP 5; ABG: pH 7.41, PaCO2 38, PaO2 95\n- **Complications**: Two episodes of mucus plugging requiring emergent suctioning; one episode of right lower lobe atelectasis (resolved with aggressive pulmonary toilet)\n- **Bowel/Bladder**: Indwelling Foley catheter; bowel program not yet established (UMN bowel pattern expected)\n- **Skin**: Intact; on alternating pressure mattress; turned every 2 hours\n- **Psychosocial**: College junior studying engineering; star athlete (swimming and water polo); parents are divorced; mother and father both involved but in conflict; younger sister is very close to patient. Patient has been mouthing "I want to die" to the night nurse on two occasions\n- **Medications**: Enoxaparin 40 mg daily, famotidine 20 mg BID, docusate 100 mg daily (via PEG -- placed day 10), albuterol nebulizer Q4H, normal saline nebulizer Q4H',
